From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Caner Altinbasak <cal@brightsign.biz>
Date: Tue, 29 Jul 2025 17:15:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix: Guard sanitizer header include with __has_include

The system Clang in Yocto scarthgap does not ship the sanitizer
runtime headers (sanitizer/common_interface_defs.h). Use
__has_include to conditionally include the header and provide
weak no-op stub implementations when it is not available.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [OE-specific]
---
 v8/src/sandbox/testing.cc | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/v8/src/sandbox/testing.cc	2026-04-27 18:44:51.471929665 +0100
+++ b/v8/src/sandbox/testing.cc	2026-04-27 18:44:51.579928845 +0100
@@ -40,7 +40,16 @@
 #if defined(V8_USE_ADDRESS_SANITIZER) || defined(V8_USE_MEMORY_SANITIZER) || \
     defined(V8_USE_UNDEFINED_BEHAVIOR_SANITIZER)
 #define V8_USE_ANY_SANITIZER 1
+#if __has_include(<sanitizer/common_interface_defs.h>)
 #include <sanitizer/common_interface_defs.h>
+#else
+// Sanitizer header not available in system toolchain - provide no-op stubs
+extern "C" {
+__attribute__((weak)) void __sanitizer_print_stack_trace(void) {}
+__attribute__((weak)) void __sanitizer_set_death_callback(
+    void (*callback)(void)) {}
+}
+#endif
 #endif
 
 #if defined(V8_ENABLE_SANDBOX) && defined(V8_ENABLE_MEMORY_CORRUPTION_API)
-- 
2.39.5
